%If $r$ lies below $s$, then $x \leq 1$ as otherwise $v_2v_{b+6}$ intersects $v_1v_5$ and $v_4v_n$ to the right of $s$ \sout{and $r$ could not be below $s$.}
%Since $n \geq 8$, we have $s=(0,y)$ for some $y \geq 0$, which implies that $x \geq 1$ as the angle at $s$ in the triangle $v_1v_2s$ is the same as the angle of the triangle $ss'v_5$.
