With the impending deployment of High-resolution Infrared Spectrograph for Exoplanet Characterization (HISPEC) at the Keck Observatory and Multi-Objective Diffraction-limited High-Resolution Infrared Spectrograph (MODHIS) at the Thirty Meter Telescope, significant enhancements in spectroscopic capabilities are anticipated~\cite{Mawet:2019eed,10.1117/12.2681522}. These instruments are expected to improve spectroscopic precision by three orders of magnitude and enable higher observation cadence, with exposures as short as $5$ minutes. Additionally, these advancements will facilitate the detection of late-type and fainter stars, which may have orbital periods shorter than that of S0-2/S2. With cooler atmospheres, these stars exhibit a rich variety of spectral lines with smaller intrinsic variance, in contrast to hot, early-type stars like S0-2/S2. In Fig.~\ref{fig:constraints}, we also present a future projection that includes a late-type star with one-tenth the semi-major axis of S0-2/S2 and a similar eccentricity of $0.8$, orbiting in the equatorial plane of the BH, with a total observation duration $10$ times longer than the data collected for S0-2/S2 in 2017 and 2018. The extension of the upper mass reach by a factor of two is enabled by the improved observational cadence, while the enhanced sensitivity primarily arises from the three orders of magnitude increase in spectral resolution.

Once $|C_\gamma| \approx 3 \times 10^{-5}$ is probed, the corresponding QCD axion parameter space could be ruled out for $f_\phi$ in the regions not already excluded by SMBH spin measurements, specifically for values below approximately  $10^{16}$\,GeV. Note that the QCD axion in these mass ranges has been extensively constrained by axion potential flipping due to the nucleon environment~\cite{Hook:2017psm,Zhang:2021mks,Balkin:2022qer,Gomez-Banon:2024oux,Gan:2025nlu}. Even in the case of ALPs with quadratic photon couplings, higher-order effects can induce ALP-nucleon interactions, potentially restricting the viable range of $f_\phi$. However, these constraints might be relaxed by the introduction of additional sectors in the model~\cite{Budnik:2020nwz,Madge:2024aot}.





