We numerically quantify this transitory regime by identifying the time $T_c$ at which the retraction speed $U(T)$ falls most sharply. In our simulations, this is given by the minimum of the derivative $dU/dT$. The duration of the transition,  $\Delta T_c$, is estimated as the full width at half maximum (FWHM) of this minimum. The resulting values of $T_c$ and $\Delta T_c$ as functions of $ \mathcal{L}$ are plotted in Fig.\,\ref{fig: t_duration}.




