We show an example of the mesh morphing process applied to a coarse mesh in Figure~\ref{fig:demo_mesh_coarse}, to demonstrate how mesh morphing affects the shape of triangular mesh cells. We see that higher $\alpha$ values result in modest stretching and compression of cells relative to the reference mesh, while smaller $\alpha$ values result in high-aspect-ratio cells in the highly compressed lower right corner of the mesh. 

