\subsection{Kolam Patterns as Directed Eulerian Graphs}

The dot connections in a Hridaya Kolam pattern can be modeled as a directed Eulerian graph, where each vertex (dot) has equal in-degree and out-degree. This structure ensures the existence of an Eulerian circuit—a path that visits every directed edge exactly once—enabling the entire pattern to be drawn in a single, uninterrupted motion.

\begin{figure}[H]
    \centering
    \includegraphics[width=0.45\textwidth]{expm4n3.png}
    \hspace{1em}
