\section{Conclusions} \label{sec:conclusion}

This article explores the connection between Hridaya Kolam designs and number theory, extending pattern generation from odd to even dot configurations using coprime-based modular sequences. By uniting mathematical structure with traditional aesthetics, we generate intricate, symmetric patterns with potential for practical and artistic applications. The approach highlights how culturally rooted designs can be formalized and expanded through algorithmic methods. Future directions include automating Kolam generation, applying these techniques to other motifs, and integrating machine learning for pattern synthesis and recognition—bridging mathematics, art, and technology in meaningful ways.\\

