\begin{abstract}
We introduce a model for the loss distribution of a credit portfolio considering a contagion mechanism for the default of names which is the result of two independent components: an \textit{infection attempt} generated by defaulting entities and a \textit{failed defence} from healthy ones. We then propose an efficient recursive algorithm for the loss distribution. Then we extend the framework with a more flexible mixture distribution to better fit real-world data. Finally, we propose an empirical application in which we price synthetic CDO tranches of the iTraxx index, finding a good fit for multiple tranches.\\
\textbf{Keywords:} Portfolio loss distribution, CDO, contagion, infection %\\ 
