The idea underlying TTE is that there are types of mathematical objects, such as real numbers, that require an infinite amount of information to be determined in a precise way.
It is therefore natural to employ machines designed to compute with infinite sequences of natural numbers (rather than finite), which are called \emph{Type-2 Machines}:

