There is no place on Earth where tigers and lions live together because they are predators of the same level. If by chance they met as random walkers, one would tear the other apart, even though they had never met before. Indeed,  until a couple of years ago even the largest US opponents, Russia and China, when they trade through the West-controlled SWIFT payment system \citet{eichengreen2024international}, the payments were realized mainly in dollars, ultimately helping the U.S. economy and particularly making its currency stronger.  In a homogeneous world where there is only a single dominant power, even the largest competitors partially pay the bill. Generally, the more countries save and trade in a country's  currency,   the stronger the currency, but also weaken the inflation shocks once the country prints new money during recessions, lockdowns, and wars. Therefore,  the dominance of the world leader is maintained not only through the country's military power but also through controlled financial and banking systems.

