\section{Data.}~In the paper we  use Allocated Reserves of Forex exchange reserves, where in a strict sense, FER includes only deposits of foreign currencies held by nationals and monetary authorities. The data are provided by the IMF, specifically claims in US dollars, Euro, Chinese RMB, Japanese yen, British pound sterling, Australian dollars, Canadian dollars, Swiss francs, and aggregated claims in other currencies. The data are listed quarterly, and in the paper we always use the last Q4 quarter. Military spending data are provided by the World Bank. The GDP data recorded annually are provided by \citet{imfdata2024}.


