\subsection{Ablation study}
We also conducted an ablation analysis to isolate which features of Gradientsys contributed most to its performance:

\begin{itemize}[left = 0em]
    \item \textbf{No Parallelism:} Tool invocations were executed sequentially. Result: latency nearly doubled to $\sim$70s, accuracy dropped slightly to 22.5\%.
    \item \textbf{No ReAct Reasoning:} Replaced the ReAct loop with a single-step planner. Accuracy dropped significantly to 12\%, indicating the necessity of iterative reasoning.
    \item \textbf{No Observability:} Disabled SSE-based feedback. Although task-level accuracy was unaffected, debugging complexity and development turnaround time worsened, suggesting the practical utility of live reasoning traces.
\end{itemize}

These results confirm that both the ReAct reasoning loop and parallel agent execution are essential for Gradientsys’s superior performance.


