\section{Method}\label{sec:method}

In this section, we present some simple building blocks and use them to construct a procedure for sampling from a tokenizer-based language model one byte at a time.
The fundamental structure of the algorithm is based on what we call the Valid Covering Tree, which is the tree of all possible valid token sequences that share a specific byte prefix and do not extend past the end of the prefix by more than one full token.
% The fundamental structure of the algorithm is based on an (infinite) tree of token sequences representing possible future tokens along with a procedure for pruning it to a reasonable \nascomment{(finite)} size.
We show the construction of the Valid Covering Tree in \cref{fig:tree}.

