\section{Experiments}\label{sec:experiments}

In our experiments, we apply \methodName{} at inference time to off-the-shelf language models.
In \cref{sec:efficiency} we show that our method has less computational overhead compared to other exact methods.
Next, in \cref{sec:language-modeling}, we show that exact methods perform better than heuristics in character-level language modeling.
Finally, we present several applications of our method to enable higher-level functions such as ensembling (\cref{sec:ensemble}) and proxy-tuning (\cref{sec:proxy-tuning}) models with mismatched tokenizers.
% Our overall approach is to leverage the scalability of our method to perform experiments that were not previously possible.

